<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#scenario/low> a cleets:Scenario ;
    rdfs:label "low scenario"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Each district follows the lower of its fitted diffusion curve and its fleet-turnover ceiling under a 16-year median scrappage age. The Wales ceiling is 92.10% of the private vehicle stock at 2045 Q4 and the constrained Wales share is 92.10%."@en ;
    cleets:medianScrappageYears 16.0 ;
    cleets:terminalTargetShare 0.921 .

<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#scenario/central> a cleets:Scenario ;
    rdfs:label "central scenario"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Each district follows the lower of its fitted diffusion curve and its fleet-turnover ceiling under a 14-year median scrappage age. The Wales ceiling is 96.23% of the private vehicle stock at 2045 Q4 and the constrained Wales share is 95.96%."@en ;
    cleets:medianScrappageYears 14.0 ;
    cleets:terminalTargetShare 0.9623 .

<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#scenario/high> a cleets:Scenario ;
    rdfs:label "high scenario"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Each district follows the lower of its fitted diffusion curve and its fleet-turnover ceiling under a 12-year median scrappage age. The Wales ceiling is 98.62% of the private vehicle stock at 2045 Q4 and the constrained Wales share is 97.76%."@en ;
    cleets:medianScrappageYears 12.0 ;
    cleets:terminalTargetShare 0.9862 .

cleets:EVAdoptionPrediction a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "EV adoption prediction"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Model output for one LAD, quarter and scenario. Not an observed value."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cleets:Observation .

<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#activity/diffusion-q2026rev> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Turnover-constrained bounded logistic diffusion" ;
    rdfs:comment "Per-LAD logistic curves (rate, midpoint) fitted independently to the quarterly matched-scope adoption share (VEH0132 private BEV / VEH0105 private licensed vehicles, all body types), 2011 Q4 to 2025 Q4, recency-weighted. The reported trajectory is the lower, in every forecast quarter, of the district's fitted curve and its own fleet-turnover ceiling (age-structured Weibull survival; pure petrol and diesel sales end 2030 Q1, hybrid sales end 2035 Q1). The low, central and high scenarios use the ceiling under 16, 14 and 12-year median scrappage ages. Counts are the share multiplied by the district's 2025 Q4 private stock; the non-battery-electric stock remaining is that stock less the predicted keepership." ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-22T08:09:49.133965+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0105>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0132> .

